      "writtenOn": "2025-11-12T19:04:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not my company\u0027s driver, `stmmac-platform` is Linux kernel driver from mainline and it has no relation to Rockchip or Telechips company specific implementation or patches. There is `CONFIG_DWMAC_ROCKCHIP\u003dm` kernel config which is part of Rockchip to integrate via `stmmac-platform`.\n\n---\n\u003e (again, a Bug: tag is needed) \n\nI read Google instruction here - https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/\n\n\u003e Requirements for Android-specific patches: `ANDROID:`\n\u003e If the patch is fixing a bug to Android-specific code\n\u003e * tag the patch subject with `ANDROID:`\n\u003e * add a `Fixes:` tag that cites the patch with the bug\n\n\n\u003e If the patch is a new feature\n\u003e * tag the patch subject with `ANDROID:`\n\u003e * add a `Bug:` tag with the Android bug (required for android-specific features)\n\nSo it must be `Fixes:`, not `Bug:`.",
      "parentUuid": "e6ef5098_fe6aeb75",
      "revId": "9fffcff899b8e6baa0f0430f736a5ba2237a47ab",
